evm version 1.15.11-stable
NAME:
   evm run - Run arbitrary evm binary

USAGE:
   evm run [command options] <code>

DESCRIPTION:
   The run command runs arbitrary EVM code.

OPTIONS:
   
    --dump                              (default: false)                  
          dumps the state after the run
   
    --statdump                          (default: false)                  
          displays stack and heap memory information

   TRACING

   
    --trace                             (default: false)                  
          Enable tracing and output trace log.
   
    --trace.format value                (default: "json")                 
          Trace output format to use (json|struct|md)
   
    --trace.nomemory, --nomemory        (default: true)                   
          disable memory output
   
    --trace.noreturndata, --noreturndata (default: true)                   
          enable return data output
   
    --trace.nostack, --nostack          (default: false)                  
          disable stack output
   
    --trace.nostorage, --nostorage      (default: false)                  
          disable storage output

   VIRTUAL MACHINE

   
    --bench                             (default: false)                  
          benchmark the execution
   
    --codefile value                                                      
          File containing EVM code. If '-' is specified, code is read from stdin
   
    --create                            (default: false)                  
          Indicates the action should be create rather than call
   
    --gas value                         (default: 10000000000)            
          Gas limit for the evm
   
    --input value                                                         
          Input for the EVM
   
    --inputfile value                                                     
          File containing input for the EVM
   
    --prestate value                                                      
          JSON file with prestate (genesis) config
   
    --price value                       (default: 0)                      
          Price set for the evm
   
    --receiver value                                                      
          The transaction receiver (execution context)
   
    --sender value                                                        
          The transaction origin
   
    --value value                       (default: 0)                      
          Value set for the evm

